WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.801
-In a few minutes,
we are going to talk

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.601
to Connecticut Senator
Chris Murphy,

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.000
which I am very grateful for,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.734
because he gave
a very powerful speech

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.267
on the Senate floor yesterday

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.868
demanding that his colleagues
take action.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.400
And I was thankful
for those words

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.267
because among many other things,

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:19.801
it reminded us
that we can't become numb.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.868
Because what is happening right
now does not have to happen.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.033
It is not inevitable.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.267
It is a choice,
a choice that our leaders

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.467
and the powerful forces
behind them have made

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.200
and are continuing
to make every day

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.033
that they refuse
to do anything at all

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.567
that could make these
horrific events less likely.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.067
America has more guns
than people.

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:38.901
We have more mass shootings by
far than any other peer nations.

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:40.634
Those two things
are obviously related.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:46.067
So now to talk a little bit more
about how we got to a place

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.801
where those two things
can be true,

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.968
it is time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.434
♪♪

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:55.601
[ Applause ]

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:58.734
Entrenched, powerful forces
have perpetrated a monumental,

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.501
decades-long fraud in convincing
large numbers of people

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.067
that it is their constitutional
right to own arsenals

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.434
and military-grade weaponry.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.300
And they've invested
large sums in convincing people

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.634
that that made-up right --

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:13.467
a right five Republican justices
essentially invented

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.934
out of whole cloth
not that long ago --

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.334
is constantly under threat.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.501
And to be clear,
that's not just my opinion.

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.000
I'm not a constitutional
scholar.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.334
I think that's clear.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.501
Constitutional scholars
do not have tiny figurines

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:29.167
of Andy Samberg on their desk
that say, "My doink fell off."

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.667
I'm not saying
they don't have them.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:35.667
I'm just saying if they do,
they're kept safely in a drawer.

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.267
So, I didn't just come up with
the take that the unregulated

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.267
right to own military-grade
weaponry is a fraud.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.601
on my own --
it was the opinion

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.033
of former Supreme Court
Chief Justice Warren Burger,

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:47.033
a conservative who said
this in 1991.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.567
-If I were writing
the Bill of Rights now,

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.567
there wouldn't be any such thing
as the Second Amendment.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.934
-Which says...

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.534
-That a well regulated militia,

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.334
being necessary for the defense
of the state,

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.133
the people's rights
to bear arms.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.467
This has been the subject

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.133
of one of the greatest
pieces of fraud --

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:08.434
I repeat the word fraud --
on the American public

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:10.501
by special interest groups

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.834
that I have ever seen
in my lifetime.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.601
Now, just look at those words.
There are only three lines

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.000
to that amendment.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.467
"A well regulated militia."

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.701
If the militia, which was going
to be the state army,

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:27.300
was going to be well regulated,
why shouldn't 16 and 17 and 18

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.501
or any other age persons
be regulated in the use of arms

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.634
the way an automobile
is regulated?

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:36.000
-First of all, it's a shock just
to see a conservative justice

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.100
say something in public without
sneering like the villain

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.601
from every '80s teen comedy.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.067
Second, he's right.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:43.367
The words "well-regulated" are
right there in the amendment.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.200
There is no mystery.
It's not Wordle

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.667
or the New York Times
Spelling Bee.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:47.834
We don't have to guess --

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.067
which, by the way,
it's what I do, guys.

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.501
After I get the easy ones,

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.100
I just start
typing in fake words

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.167
and hoping they're real.
Moaxy?

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.634
Is moaxy a word?

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.667
Let me try 30 more times.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:02:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.501
The idea that
the Second Amendment

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:04.467
guarantees an individual's
unregulated right to own

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:07.300
an arsenal of military-grade
weaponry is so insane

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.300
and was shrugged off
as ridiculous for so long.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.501
Then, in 1982,

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:14.100
Senate Republicans
went to the absurd lengths

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.801
of issuing a report that claimed
to have discovered

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.701
"clear and long-lost proof

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.367
that the Second Amendment
was intended as an individual

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.767
right of the American citizen
to keep and carry arms."

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.033
It is absolutely insane

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.934
that Republicans claim
to have found long-lost proof

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:32.400
that changed the meaning
of a document written in 1787,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.801
in 1982, which means --

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.601
definitely means
one of them had just seen

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.033
"Raiders of the Lost Ark"
and then said,

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.701
"You know, sometimes
people find old [bleep]

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.868
I'm just saying."

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.701
I mean, how'd it go?
Did Nicolas Cage find a secret

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:48.000
Post-it Note hidden
inside the Liberty Bell?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.033
We were so focused on the crack,
we never looked inside!

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:52.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.467
But that should give you an idea
of how preposterous

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.300
and unhinged this whole idea is.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.334
The side that claims to care

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.234
about the plain language
of the Constitution

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.901
and the original meaning
of the Founding Fathers

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.033
had to pretend
to unearth some secret,

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.968
hidden proof
that the Second Amendment

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.067
actually means
something completely different

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.501
from what it obviously says,
which is totally divorced

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.167
from how other sane countries
deal with these kind of horrors.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:18.367
Australia, the UK,
New Zealand, Norway --

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.801
they've all responded
to mass shootings

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.133
with stricter gun laws

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:24.634
or campaigns
to confiscate or buy back guns.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.734
And those laws have worked
because again,

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.300
there is an obvious correlation

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.100
between how many guns
we have in this country

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.133
and how many gun deaths we have.
And by the way,

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.033
when local governments
have tried gun buyback programs

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:38.234
on a small scale here in the US,
they've often been successful.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:39.767
In fact, just a few days ago,

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.434
the police department
in Sacramento

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:44.734
held a gun buyback event in
exchange for $50 gas gift cards.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.734
The event, which was supposed
to last for five hours,

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.501
got more takers than expected.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.801
The department announced
just 45 minutes into the event

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:53.133
that it had exhausted
its supply of gift cards

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.567
due to overwhelming response.
I'm not surprised.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:59.801
You know what I'd give up for
a $50 gas gift card right now?

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.701
Half a tank?!

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.801
That's why I dress
like this right now.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:07.667
I gave all my suits back
as part of a buyback program,

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:11.767
and now I don't have to pay
for gas for another week.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.067
I also gave up haircuts,
which is why I'm now

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.501
on an ongoing mission
to get cast

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:19.000
in the next Marvel movie
as Old Loki.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.033
I think I can do it.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.567
Because I look, like...

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:30.067
5 to 10 months older
than Tom Hiddleston.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:34.434
But even more revealing than
the success of the event itself

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:38.000
were the reasons people gave
for turning in these guns.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.133
Among other reasons, community
members most commonly cited

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.834
a lack of experience
or knowledge with firearms,

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:46.234
lack of knowledge
of the legality of firearms,

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:49.501
or an inability to safely store
the firearms

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:51.834
as the main reasons for
participating in the exchange.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.801
It turns out some people
don't even want these guns

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.234
and would like
to get rid of them.

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:59.100
Imagine if we launch
a national campaign like that

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.000
or like what Australia did
in the '90s

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.734
when it confiscated
650,000 guns,

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.934
and as a result,
gun deaths plummeted.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:08.400
Of course, in Australia they
didn't give out gas gift cards,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.834
they gave out Foster's
because, you know,

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:11.300
it's Australian for beer.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.467
Real talk, though --

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:14.067
they don't drink Foster's
in Australia.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.868
"Foster's --
it's Australian for beer"

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:17.067
is just a marketing lie

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:19.067
they invented
to try to sell it to us,

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:20.801
and they used Crocodile Dundee
to do it.

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.767
I trusted you, Croc!

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.701
I trusted you,
and you lied to me.

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:27.534
"Fosters -- it's Australian
for beer" would be like

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:30.067
if I were in a commercial
on Australian TV

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:33.400
where I said, "Arby's --
it's American for steak."

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.300
Or if Republican senators

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.133
said they claimed
to have discovered

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.167
clear and long-lost proof
that the Second Amendment said

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:42.100
everyone is allowed
to have all the guns they want,

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.267
in that it's obvious bull[bleep]
because again, as we've seen,

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:48.100
gun safety measures
like assault weapons bans

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.400
and gun buyback programs
have worked.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.901
They have worked
in other countries.

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.601
When we've tried them,
they've worked here, too.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:57.167
Our gun production and ownership
rates are simply off the charts,

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.868
incomparable
to any other nation on Earth.

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.601
And as a result,
so are our gun deaths.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:04.067
It's within our power
to stop this,

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:06.400
and allowing these massacres
to continue is,

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.834
in fact, a choice,

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.534
as Connecticut Senator
Chris Murphy

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.801
said in a speech
on the Senate floor yesterday.

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:14.501
-What are we doing?

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:16.334
Why do you spend all this time

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:18.701
running for
the United States Senate?

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:23.000
Why do you go through all
the hassle of getting this job,

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.701
of putting yourself
in a position of authority?

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:28.868
If your answer is that
as this slaughter increases,

00:07:28.868 --> 00:07:32.067
as our kids run for their lives,
we do nothing.

00:07:34.801 --> 00:07:37.300
What are we doing?

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:40.567
Why are you here?

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:44.701
I'm here on this floor to beg --

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:47.200
to literally get down
on my hands and knees

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.501
and beg my colleagues.

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.534
Find a path forward here.

00:07:53.534 --> 00:07:55.701
Work with us

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:58.901
to find a way to pass laws

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.434
that make this less likely.

00:08:01.434 --> 00:08:05.634
-This is a moment, if you are
a person in a position of power,

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.534
to ask yourself what
you're doing to stop this.

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:09.367
Because he's right.
Why are you there?

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:11.667
Why else are you
in the United States Senate?

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:13.868
Unless it's to raise money
and give speeches

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:15.300
and dole out favors

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.400
and ride that secret little
train in the Capitol basement

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.067
that looks like
the railroad to Disneyland,

00:08:19.067 --> 00:08:21.434
except instead of dropping you
off at the Magic Kingdom,

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:23.934
it brings you
to Lindsey Graham's office.

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:25.501
[ As Graham ]
My office is like a castle,

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:28.467
in that my meemaw calls me
a little Prince Charming.

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:30.200
[ Normal voice ]
And yet, maddeningly,

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.367
there are those who claim

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:34.367
to support
popular gun safety measures

00:08:34.367 --> 00:08:36.367
but aren't actually
willing to use their power

00:08:36.367 --> 00:08:37.534
to get those measures passed,

00:08:37.534 --> 00:08:39.467
like West Virginia
Senator Joe Manchin.

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:41.601
CNN reported yesterday
that Manchin says he would do

00:08:41.601 --> 00:08:45.334
"anything I can" to move common
sense gun legislation forward,

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:47.801
but still refused to eliminate
the filibuster

00:08:47.801 --> 00:08:49.667
to get gun legislation
through the Senate.

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:52.100
Then you're not willing
to do anything you can!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.901
It's like if you told
your spouse you're willing to do

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:56.734
anything to clean the dishes
except get up from the couch.

00:08:56.734 --> 00:08:57.968
"I can do it from here

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:00.167
if you tie a sponge
to a long stick."

00:09:00.167 --> 00:09:01.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:03.367
If you're willing to live
with these horrors,

00:09:03.367 --> 00:09:04.534
then just say that.

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:05.901
Just say you're willing to.

00:09:05.901 --> 00:09:08.901
But don't hide behind
a bull[bleep] procedural rule

00:09:08.901 --> 00:09:11.133
that, by the way,
is not in the Constitution

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:13.234
and didn't even exist when
the Senate was created anyway.

00:09:13.234 --> 00:09:15.133
You guys all act
like the Constitution

00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:17.367
has an entire section
on the filibuster,

00:09:17.367 --> 00:09:20.200
when the word isn't even
so much as mentioned once.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.200
Maybe we need to get Nick Cage
to burst into Manchin's office

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.834
with a secret piece
of parchment screaming, "Joe!

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.634
I found a note from John Adams
in the Lincoln Memorial's taint!

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:31.267
He said the filibuster
is bull[bleep]"

00:09:31.267 --> 00:09:34.334
No, of course, Nick Cage
would never agree to do that.

00:09:34.334 --> 00:09:37.968
But what about someone who does
an excellent impression of him?

00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:41.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.234 --> 00:09:45.567
Just think about it.

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:47.767
And by the way,
this is the same Senate

00:09:47.767 --> 00:09:50.968
that moved with the speed
of a Saturn V rocket

00:09:50.968 --> 00:09:53.501
to get Supreme Court justices
more security

00:09:53.501 --> 00:09:55.567
when some people were picketing
outside their homes.

00:09:55.567 --> 00:09:58.167
So that should give you
a sense of their priorities.

00:09:58.167 --> 00:10:00.734
When they do want
to protect someone,

00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:02.734
they're capable
of doing it quickly.

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:04.734
And while the Manchins and
Mitch McConnells of the world

00:10:04.734 --> 00:10:07.701
are offering their empty words
and refusing to take action,

00:10:07.701 --> 00:10:10.667
the most depraved people
in our politics are suggesting

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.300
that instead of doing
the obvious thing

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.100
that many other countries
have done successfully,

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.000
which is to simply pass laws

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.734
regulating the number of guns
in the country

00:10:17.734 --> 00:10:19.501
and the ability
to easily get them,

00:10:19.501 --> 00:10:23.334
we should instead arm teachers
and essentially turn schools

00:10:23.334 --> 00:10:25.200
into fortified military bases.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.701
-The most effective tool
for keeping kids safe

00:10:28.701 --> 00:10:31.334
is armed law enforcement
on the campus.

00:10:31.334 --> 00:10:35.267
-People, retired military,
retired law enforcement

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:39.634
outside the perimeter
of every school in the country.

00:10:39.634 --> 00:10:41.467
They can donate their time.
They can --

00:10:41.467 --> 00:10:44.701
We can offer them tax breaks,
no income tax in the state,

00:10:44.701 --> 00:10:47.834
no income tax federally,
10 hours a week.

00:10:47.834 --> 00:10:50.334
And we could have every school
in America covered.

00:10:50.334 --> 00:10:51.767
-We have to harden these targets

00:10:51.767 --> 00:10:55.100
so no one can get in, ever,
except through one entrance.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.100
-What we need to do
is utilize smart technology.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.434
That's what's needed.
We need to install man traps.

00:11:01.434 --> 00:11:03.400
This is something
we've discussed in the past,

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.067
back in 2018 -- I checked.

00:11:05.067 --> 00:11:06.400
Man traps,

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:09.200
a series of interlocking doors
at the school entrance

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.100
that are triggered
by a tripwire.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.534
-We can't stop bad people
from doing bad things.

00:11:13.534 --> 00:11:15.133
They're gonna violate
murder laws,

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:16.334
they're not gonna follow
gun laws.

00:11:16.334 --> 00:11:18.167
I've never understood
that argument.

00:11:18.167 --> 00:11:19.801
But we are -- we can harden
these schools.

00:11:19.801 --> 00:11:21.634
We can create points of access

00:11:21.634 --> 00:11:23.033
that are difficult
to get through.

00:11:23.033 --> 00:11:27.334
We can potentially arm
and prepare and train teachers

00:11:27.334 --> 00:11:29.901
and other administrators
to respond quickly.

00:11:29.901 --> 00:11:31.367
-Are you out of your
[bleep] mind?

00:11:31.367 --> 00:11:33.868
You guys want to turn schools
into maximum security prisons

00:11:33.868 --> 00:11:35.701
with man traps and tripwires

00:11:35.701 --> 00:11:37.367
and teachers carrying guns?

00:11:37.367 --> 00:11:38.701
If these people had their way,

00:11:38.701 --> 00:11:40.801
everything would be a scene
out of [bleep] "RoboCop."

00:11:40.801 --> 00:11:43.934
There are truly no words
for how grotesque this is.

00:11:43.934 --> 00:11:46.501
They want to arm teachers
and yet they're not even willing

00:11:46.501 --> 00:11:49.067
to throw enough money at schools
to get them history books

00:11:49.067 --> 00:11:51.534
that don't end with the fall
of the Berlin Wall.

00:11:51.534 --> 00:11:52.868
And that's...
[ Applause ]

00:11:52.868 --> 00:11:54.534
And that's, right there...

00:11:54.534 --> 00:11:57.133
[ Applause continues ]

00:11:57.133 --> 00:12:01.367
Kids, that's how Ronald Reagan
saved democracy.

00:12:01.367 --> 00:12:03.300
If you want to know
what happened after that,

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.467
get into college.

00:12:04.467 --> 00:12:06.901
And to the people
who cynically parrot

00:12:06.901 --> 00:12:09.267
the mindless talking point
that advocates for gun reform

00:12:09.267 --> 00:12:11.567
are somehow politicizing this --
what else?

00:12:11.567 --> 00:12:14.434
What else is politics for?
It's a crisis.

00:12:14.434 --> 00:12:16.634
And this is what
our political system

00:12:16.634 --> 00:12:19.067
is supposed to do --
address the crisis.

00:12:19.067 --> 00:12:21.901
If that's all you can muster
in the wake of this horror,

00:12:21.901 --> 00:12:24.934
that tired, empty mantra,
then you need to look inward

00:12:24.934 --> 00:12:27.367
because we can --
we can do something.

00:12:27.367 --> 00:12:29.467
We know from our experience,
our own experience,

00:12:29.467 --> 00:12:30.901
and from the experiences
of other countries,

00:12:30.901 --> 00:12:31.901
it's possible.

00:12:31.901 --> 00:12:33.367
It has not always been
like this.

00:12:33.367 --> 00:12:35.167
It doesn't always have to be
like this.

00:12:35.167 --> 00:12:36.567
We can change things.

00:12:36.567 --> 00:12:40.067
And if you're a person in a
position of power, you must act.

00:12:40.067 --> 00:12:42.734
Because if you choose
to spend this moment

00:12:42.734 --> 00:12:44.100
in the wake of this horror

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.000
using your power to do nothing,
then you are a...

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.801
-Fraud.
I repeat the word fraud.

00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:51.534
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:51.534 --> 00:12:55.300
♪♪

